  "2026-08-21T12:56:15.501Z","harness:codex","Second-review implementation and verification 2026-08-21: resolved terminal alias parity, advisory-only terminal debt tokens, active versus terminal graph summary counts, relation-only hierarchy indexing, dangling scalar-parent filtering, and cycle-tree leaf retention. The collector is public through the graph SDK barrel; read paths no longer pay defect-analysis cost. Isolated full verification passed 547 files / 7,677 tests with exact 100% statements 56170/56170, branches 41920/41920, functions 11682/11682, and lines 54169/54169. TMPDIR=/var/tmp pnpm quality:static passed repository assurance, SDK/package parity, command and flag grammar, refusal closure, tracker-context quality, graph composition, record integrity, SDK cost, and transport floors."
  "2026-08-21T13:20:37.291Z","harness:codex","Exact-head review recurrence: CodeRabbit reviewed 20e4a7a9d and opened 13 threads. Valid hierarchy-integrity scope includes partial-debt repair monotonicity, malformed dependency resilience, assembly copy retention, bounded health output, early update-lock release, canonical tree parent IDs, registry defaults, and fixture proof. Reopened and claimed only while actively implementing these fixes."
  "2026-08-21T14:09:40.722Z","harness:codex","Third-review completion evidence 2026-08-21: all 13 CodeRabbit exact-head findings were verified and addressed on their original inline threads. The SDK now keeps active extension relationship registries as the omitted-argument default, retains hierarchy analysis across spread-copied assemblies, rejects malformed dependency input without crashing, bounds health relation evidence, permits monotonic partial repair of legacy cycle/cardinality debt, and releases the workspace writer lock immediately after durable persistence. Definitive isolated coverage passed 547 files and 7,680 tests at exact 100% statements 56180/56180, branches 41936/41936, functions 11686/11686, and lines 54178/54178. TMPDIR=/var/tmp pnpm quality:static passed the complete repository, docstring, duplication, package, SDK, grammar, refusal, tracker-context, graph-composition, record-integrity, and transport gates."
