learnings[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-21T05:34:29.917Z","harness:codex","Hierarchy integrity must be normalized from registry direction and child-end cardinality before any consumer reasons about ancestors, descendants, cycles, or rollups. Mutation checks should compare before/after defect identities so legacy debt stays repairable while new debt fails closed. Terminal-only defects belong in visible advisory findings, not health failure state."
  "2026-08-21T14:09:41.765Z","harness:codex","Public graph analysis attached only through object identity is not a stable SDK contract because consumers routinely spread or serialize assemblies. Preserve derived contracts on the public assembly value, keep workspace registry resolution in a dependency-cycle-free module, and compare defect sets monotonically so a repair that shrinks legacy debt remains allowed."
